      "severity": "P2",
      "path": "skills/international/north-macedonia/north-macedonia-income-tax.md",
      "line": 68,
      "title": "Separate the domestic securities annual assessment route from ordinary monthly e-PDD",
      "source": "https://www.ujp.gov.mk/files/attachment/0000/1466/ZAKON_ZA_DANOKOT_NA_LICEN_DOHOD_-_Azuriran_so_Sl.vesnik____274___od_20.12.2022.pdf",
      "provision": "PIT arts.85-a,87(1)(2),91-a,93(4), PDF pp.25-29",
      "problem": "The filing section gives only the general monthly self-assessment timetable and does not explain the specific domestic securities/fund assessment machinery for the gains already covered in the base. This leaves a reader without the correct filer, annual assessment date or payment trigger.",
      "fix": "State that the Central Securities Depository/fund managers report by 15 January next year, UJP assesses using the statutory reports by 15 February, and assessed tax is due within 15 days of service. Distinguish foreign receipts requiring self-reporting under arts.87-88 from this domestic reporting route. Do not imply that every security sale is a monthly domestic self-assessed sale.",
      "requires_closure": true
    },
